 "dependency_review": "Inspected the intake row (notion_id 3b731704-6eeb-81c8-aa30-dea039430b25, recording 2026-09-21 15-14-38, lane 'icon choreography', topic 'Hermes can now help you inside any application you are working on: Hub mode sits on top of the app and pulls its context in real time'), the approved plan, context and scene handoff, and the TITLE constant of the approved split generator ('Hermes Hub mode sits on any app'), which the split and cutout index.html also carry and is the package title. The three editable projects each carry index.html; every local src/href resolves inside its tree (checked file by file, none climbs out), and the whiteboard assets folder is a symlink into stage/hermeshub_whiteboard that delivery materializes as real files. Generators: hermeshub_scene.py, the split, cutout (plus envelope) and whiteboard generators and _hermeshub_proof.py; their imports resolve to pipeline/captions.py, pipeline/pointing_cues.py, formats/cutout/lib (cutout_core, cutout_depthfield) and formats/whiteboard/lib (whiteboard_build, whiteboard_fix6_core), all included; the rest is stdlib, numpy, PIL and playwright. Media and timing: the raw recording, its full ASR transcript, the whole cuts/hermeshub set (master, face plates, audio, EDL, tight transcript) and the seven prep stage records. Matting: the matting/hermeshub session (v1 alpha, v5 alpha/cut/rim layers, plates, chair prompt and audit, selection, measurements, cache, matting.json); there is no matting_fallback session. Config and paperwork: every gen/_*hermeshub* build, BiRefNet master, cue, envelope, gate, geometry, prerender, pill-width, QC, render-control, spec and whiteboard record. Review: final_hermeshub.json (Miguel approval on the staged videos), agent start/done/state records, the Astra matte prompt, log and result, matte review, proof crops, sheets and legacy phone records (the Astra pid file is omitted as transient). External runtime dependencies recorded, not vendored: GSAP from jsDelivr and Google Fonts at render time, HyperFrames CLI, Playwright Chromium and ffmpeg. No secrets and no other Short files."
